 =?UTF-8?q?in=20the=20grouped=20sidebar?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
- Active threads under a project header in the grouped sidebar (Group threads by project, the boringSidebarEnabled client setting) render with the same card as the flat list: project favicon and name, status with working duration, Snooze, labelled Settle, Discard draft, title and the machine, branch, pull request and provider line. The header stays their keyboard-navigation parent; drag to the composer, sweep actions, jump hints, file drop, the pinned, snoozed and settled sections and empty pinned folders behave as before.
- A card under a project header is indented by the header's favicon size plus its gap (1rem + 0.625rem = 1.625rem), so the card's project favicon starts where the header's project name starts. The indent is a margin on the card's list item, so the row's hover, active, selected, draft, file-drop and drag surfaces start at the indent too; the card keeps its height, content and actions and its title has less width.
- The header favicon size, the header gap and the indent come from three root CSS properties (--sidebar-folder-icon-size, --sidebar-folder-gap and --sidebar-folder-child-indent, their sum); the header renders with the same values as before.
- Pinned cards above the folders, the flat list, the Working shelf, and the snoozed and settled rows keep their position: only rows rendered with a folder as their navigation parent are indented.
- Nothing positions against a card's left edge: dragging is restricted to the vertical axis, the context-drag test uses the list bounds, the list motion clones a removed row at its own offsetLeft and width, and the keyboard context menu opens at the row's own left edge, which is now the indented edge.
- The Labs sub-setting Two-line folder rows and its settings search entry are removed; the sidebar no longer reads boringSidebarMultilineRows. The contract field is unchanged, and the folder and folder-multiline variants stay in SidebarThreadRow.tsx, no longer selected by the sidebar.
- The open project headers follow the project icon order through the same shared sort as the icon row (sortSidebarProjectGroups with Project icon order and, under Manual, the manual ranks): pinned first, then by name, latest activity or the manual order, so the headers and the icons always agree. Archived project headers stay after them. Under Name and Manual a thread update does not reorder the headers. The upstream Project order setting still governs the project picker and the command palette.
- Alt-click on a project header collapses every header when the clicked one is expanded and expands every header when it is collapsed. Alt+Enter and Alt+Space on a focused header do the same and suppress the plain toggle. A plain click toggles only that header. The bulk change is one write of every folder's expansion keys through the persisted project expansion state.
- A collapsed header shows the project icon row's badge instead of the status dot: the count of hidden threads needing attention (every badge state except Working, 1-9 or 9+), the most urgent state's colour, a plain dot when only Working threads are hidden and nothing when no state applies. It counts the hidden threads with the same per-thread derivation as the project row badges, including Woke and local visit fallbacks. The muted thread count, chevron and hover New thread button stay, and screen-reader text states the per-state counts.
- The collapsed-header badge counts woke threads against the same clock that placed them: the latest snooze wake among the threads that is not later than the partition's current time, or the snooze wake clock when no wake has passed. The value changes only when a wake passes.
- Folder headers skip Sidebar renders that change neither their hidden threads nor a passed wake deadline (holding or releasing a modifier key, for example): the toggle callback is stable, the header's memo compares its hidden threads member by member, and with the machine filter narrowed to one machine the rebuilt project group snapshots are cached apart from the Sidebar's per-render state, so they keep their identity while their inputs are unchanged.
- The badge is one shared component with its own stylesheet; the project row positions it over icons, +N and popup icons, and the header shows it inline. The folder-dot helper and its class and label maps are removed.
- The Project icon order row description and its settings search terms say that the order also applies to project folders while threads are grouped. The user guide describes full cards in folders, the folder order, Alt-click and Alt+Enter, and the collapsed-header badge.

Integration details:
- The folder and folder-multiline row variants are no longer rendered by the sidebar, so the grouped-row Snooze added to those variants by 😴 Snooze threads from grouped sidebar rows is not reachable; grouped rows get Snooze from the card.
- On touch screens the always-visible New thread button can overlap the left edge of the collapsed-header badge by about 3 px; the status dot sat in the same place.

Port to 20c3dd3689:
- Upstream 6f8c7433d0 added defaultProjectFallbackReady to the useHandleNewThread result; the grouped-sidebar browser test mock sets it to true like the existing header test.

